==Results==
The second round of the elections was held on 19 April between [[José Ramos-Horta]], a former [[President of Timor-Leste|president]], and the incumbent [[Francisco Guterres]]. In the runoff Ramos-Horta prevailed with 62% of the vote.<ref>{{Cite news |date=April 20, 2022 |title=Ramos-Horta wins Timor-Leste presidential election |pages=1 |work=The Star |url=https://www.thestar.com.my/aseanplus/aseanplus-news/2022/04/20/ramos-horta-wins-timor-leste-presidential-election |access-date=April 20, 2022 |archive-date=21 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220421074713/https://www.thestar.com.my/aseanplus/aseanplus-news/2022/04/20/ramos-horta-wins-timor-leste-presidential-election |url-status=live }}</ref>

